{
  "bridge_text": "While Lina believes a small kindness can open doors better than shadows, the apple rests on the step as a token of peace. Mosk watches it, his decision made as he begins his slow descent into the roots.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, perhaps wondering if such a small gift could truly mend a heavy heart. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. He beckoned for Lina to follow as they disappeared into the shadows of the trunk."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the firefly resting on that soft, velvet-green carpet of moss, the air grew still. Mosk watched her, his heart heavy with the memory of that long-ago winter.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming was a quiet song. A firefly the size of a robin lay nestled on a bed of moss, that soft, velvet-green blanket that kept the ground so cozy for a weary traveler. Her glow was fading fast. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he remembered their friendship and the winter he arrived too late with medicine. He had guarded this tree ever since, too ashamed to look her in the eye."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk the fox watching her from his perch, Lina stood firm against the shadows of the trunk. She knew the secret of the humming was waiting just below.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Mosk told her, in a voice like dry leaves, that the tree was not for visiting and that she should go home and forget the humming. Lina stood her ground, whispering that she could not forget what she had not yet heard."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed sternly at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket for the last apple of the season. She set the fruit on the step between them and offered it as a gift for his trouble. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, then stood up, tightened his vest, and began to climb down the stairs without a single word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
