{
  "bridge_text": "With that apple tucked safely away, the grumpy fox seemed to have shed his heavy silence. He led the way down, leaving the shadows of the doorway behind.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming deepened into a soft, melodic song. There, resting on a bed of moss, lay a firefly as large as a robin, her golden light flickering dangerously low. Mosk’s whiskers trembled with sudden sorrow as he whispered that she had once been his closest friend, but long ago, he had failed to bring her medicine. He had guarded the tree in silence ever since, too ashamed to face the friend he had let down."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the glowing creature and asked what would mend her spirit. The queen whispered that a drop of warm milk and a kind word were the only medicine she had ever truly needed. Mosk hurried to fetch the milk in a tiny silver thimble, placing his paw gently beside hers. As the queen’s light steadied, the tree’s humming transformed into a beautiful, new tune, and for the first time in many years, Mosk hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The curtain of pride is indeed heavy, but the tune humming through the branches now begins to lift it. Let us see how the forest listens as the queen finds her strength.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed, sensing that even Mosk’s quiet pride could not hide the truth of this moment. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers, finally letting his guard down. The queen's glow steadied, and the humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before—a song that invited Mosk, for the first time in years, to hum along."
    }
  ],
